 lines=['# R320 — derived closed staircase; packing tradeoffs and measured cost','', '**No reconstruction is adopted. Stop for review; no automatic R321.**', '',f'The new model derives winding, minor radius and hole-axis orientation from count, radius, thickness and the actual closed staircase. The best near-rise diagnostic has conditional Emax **{best["emax"]:.3f}px**, versus R319 **{old["emax"]:.3f}px** under its different frozen map. Its diameter is only **{c["diameter_photo_px"]:.2f}px**, compared with the fixed uncertain photo reference33.468px, and pigment omission is **{100*best["geometry"]["material_omission"]:.1f}%**. The discrepancy is {best['emax']/D:.3f} fixed photo diameters and {best['emax']/c['diameter_photo_px']:.3f} fitted diameters. This is a physically constrained pilot with visible geometric deficiencies, not a better reconstruction or a recovered bead count.','', '[Photographic review](r320/results/index.html) · [Specification](R320_SPECIFICATION.md) · [Reproduction](R320_REPRODUCE.md) · [Performance JSON](r320/results/performance.json) · [Cost plan](r320/results/optimization-plan.json)','', '## Physical interpretation and equations','', 'The identical legacy bead is the rounded annular cross-section from `beads.pov`: major cross-section radius0.57r, flat half-width0.086r, rounding radius0.344r and axial stretch (0.7/0.43)a. Its exact radial support is r and axial half-support is0.7ra, hence **H=1.4ra**, not a redefined axial parameter. Hole fraction0.14 and roundedness0.8 are fixed. The original macros also illustrate other profiles/materials; R320 uses one shared rigid shape.', '', 'For each integer N, W=floor(N/6.5+0.5), T=N/W, R0=r/sin(pi/T), P=L/W. The ideal signed tilt is -hand atan(H/(2πR0)). The implemented axis is the normalized cross product of the radial direction and the actual helical center-trajectory tangent, with its sign chosen toward the major tangent. Thus it is normal to the local staircase surface, not aligned with a hypothetical thread. On a straight major axis this gives -hand atan(P/(2πR)); on a curved axis the normal also includes the local major curvature. Independent analytic differentiation checks this construction.', '', 'The POV expression is r=0.96 R sin(pi/6.5), so R=r/[0.96 sin(pi/6.5)]: **4.167% larger**, not smaller, than the ideal radius. This is an empirical placement allowance, not an independently fitted material constant. POV major length gives P=1.05×1.3r=1.365r, so P/H=0.975 for its height0.7 profile. Its object rotations keep the hole axis on the major tangent; it does not implement the derived staircase tilt. The old file is preserved byte-for-byte.', '', 'The photographic centerline and fixed R319 camera establish L in historical units. Camera scale stays8.658283442409605px/unit, so 2r×scale is the actual explored image diameter. Allowing radius and camera scale to rescale together would introduce a similarity gauge; this pilot deliberately holds that gauge fixed. Elevation, roll and common light are inherited nuisance assumptions, not calibrated constants. Perspective is set from the inherited negligible value to zero.', '', 'A deterministic contact construction starts at R0, tests increasing factors1.02/1.04/1.08/1.12/1.16 when necessary, then bisects the first successful bracket eight times. It uses the exact shared support function and all spatial pairs; actual annular-volume fallback distinguishes demonstrated penetration from unresolved convex-envelope failure. This is a sufficient construction, **not proof of a global minimum packing radius** or monotonic feasibility. No minor radius is adjusted to fit photograph errors. All refinement factors and failed brackets are retained.', '', 'The primary near-rise screen is **0.90≤L/(WH)≤1.15**, explicitly an exploration budget, not measured crochet tolerance. Wider ratios remain labeled diagnostic controls. No large rise violation is hidden in the objective. At fixed count/camera/centerline, thicker beads reduce this ratio and can intersect; smaller beads improve clearance but lose pigment coverage. An exact mechanical packing/equilibrium law remains absent.', '', '## Closed topology, seam and correction budgets','', f'The selected model has N={c["count"]}, W={c["winding"]}, T={c["turn"]:.8f}, r={c["radius"]:.6f}, axial={c["axial"]:.6f}, H={c["H"]:.6f}, L={c["length"]:.6f}, R/R0={c["minor_ratio"]:.6f}, **L/(WH)={c["circumference_ratio"]:.6f}**. Ideal signed tilt={c["ideal_tilt_deg"]:.4f}°, actual curvature-aware range={c["actual_tilt_min_deg"]:.4f}…{c["actual_tilt_max_deg"]:.4f}°. Derived tilt is stored in the frames; the unused legacy scalar tilt is zero.', '', '`topology=closed`, `gap_steps=0`, fixed `seam_fraction=-0.5`; no seam/gap/turn/tilt/compact_tilt/cant fitting. Signed addresses start at ceil(-N/2). Bead0 retains the original photo reference station and phase convention as N changes. Global phase/station registration moves actual geometry; it never relabels the index origin. The first/last pair and offset6/7 seam-crossing pairs receive the same spatial scrutiny as interiors. Additional N2401/2402 controls cross W369→370, with no index reset.', '', f'All inherited centerline/phase/spacing fields were reset before this experiment. Their previous totals were **{inh["axis_max_px"]:.3f}px** centerline displacement, **{inh["phase_max_deg"]:.2f}°** local phase, **{inh["station_max_departure_px"]:.3f}px** integrated station departure and **{inh["local_spacing_rate_max_percent"]:.3f}%** local spacing-rate departure. R319 also had translation{inh["registration_translation_px"]}px and station{inh["registration_station_px"]:.3f}px. These are total inherited departures, not just the last round’s increments.', '', f'Following the user’s centerline steering, four coefficients describe two periodic normal-displacement harmonics. Maximum total displacement is capped at3.3468px (0.10 fixed photoD); selected total is **{c["axis_correction_px"]:.4f}px**. Local minor-phase correction=0° and local spacing correction=0%. Global station is bounded±3.3468px, translation remains zero. Centerline, radius, axial, global phase and station are probed jointly; camera and lighting are not fitted. Every resulting L/(WH) is recomputed.', '', '## Search coverage and photographic results','', f'The first structured grid evaluates **{len(physical)}** inputs: nine counts2000…3200 (including2404/2405/2406), radii1.35/1.65/1.95/2.25 and axial0.65/0.85/1.05/1.25, both hands. Implied coarse diameters23.38…38.96px. Outcomes: {dict(counts)}; **{sum(r["eligible"] for r in physical)}** satisfy both certification and the near-rise screen. These are input-vector counts; internal contact-construction probes are separately serialized in each history.', '', f'The optical pilot records **{search["trial_count"]}** trials with per-count/hand frozen maps, joint radius/axial grids, bounded centerline controls and small registration probes. A further **{coupled["trials"]}** coupled trials use bilateral sensitivities and local minimax steps across counts2800,2600,2200, retaining missing predictions and physical failures. The first local refinement also included nearly adjacent2404/2405 counts; these are explicitly redundant local controls, not independent broad basins. Actual parameter ranges and every outcome remain in the serialized trial directories.', '', 'All comparisons retain the identical22 photo-only observed principal half-maximum centroids:7 black,11 red,4 yellow. Each count/hand map is initialized from one-to-one observed-bright-support overlap without predicted reflection distances, then frozen throughout its fitting epoch. Unsupported assignments remain provisional and difficult observations are never dropped. Missing predictions make Emax infinite. Full benchmark cohorts contain40/74/754 eligible automatic observations in fixed baseline geography; the full1217 detection catalog and all historical811 measurements remain unchanged. The broader automatic benchmark cohort has not received the same compact-cohort scientific review, so its errors are diagnostic.', '', '| Model | Emax px | L/(WH) | Dmodel px | Pigment omitted | Color seam conflicts | Dual distinct-color claims | Bracket p95 px |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 lines.append(f'| R319 baseline | {old["emax"]:.3f} | {old['summary']['circumference_ratio']:.4f} (nominal W; open) | {old['summary']['diameter_photo_px']:.2f} | {100*old["geometry"]["material_omission"]:.1f}% | {100*old["geometry"]["seam_conflict_fraction"]:.1f}% | {old["geometry"]["dual_count"]} | {fmt(old["geometry"]["bracket_p95"])} |')
 for m in models:
  g=m['geometry'];s=m['summary'];lines.append(f'| {m["label"]} | {m["emax"]:.3f} | {s["circumference_ratio"]:.4f} | {s["diameter_photo_px"]:.2f} | {100*g["material_omission"]:.1f}% | {100*g["seam_conflict_fraction"]:.1f}% | {g["dual_count"]} | {fmt(g["bracket_p95"])} |')
 colorrows={}
 for label in ['R319','derived-best','centerline-control','derived-2600']:
  rr=read(OUT/('R319-baseline.json.gz' if label=='R319' else label+'-model.json.gz'))
