 doc=f'''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>R320 derived closed staircase</title><style>body{{max-width:1100px;margin:30px auto;padding:0 18px;font:17px/1.5 system-ui;color:#24313b;background:#faf9f5}}img{{max-width:100%;height:auto}}section{{margin:32px 0}}a{{color:#146b85}}</style><h1>R320 — derived closed staircase</h1><p><b>No adoption. Stop for review.</b> Near-rise packing currently favors undersized beads and loses photographed pigment coverage. Different count families have provisional frozen maps.</p><p><a href="../../R320_REPORT.md">Scientific report</a> · <a href="performance.json">Measured performance</a> · <a href="optimization-plan.json">Future cost plan</a> · <a href="verification.json">Independent verification</a></p><p>Cyan: modeled visible owner edges. Yellow circles: observed reflections. Magenta crosses: predicted reflections. White vectors: discrepancies. Model holes/occlusions are shown; no black photographic boundaries are invented.</p><section><h2>Original photograph crop</h2><img src="original-crop.png"></section><section><h2>R319 comparison · {old['emax']:.3f}px, old map</h2><img src="R319-overlay.png"></section>{cards}<section><h2>Physical search</h2><img src="physical-search.png"></section><section><h2>Measured evaluation cost</h2><img src="performance.png"></section>'''
